Threshold 18; strict flags 1/20. Value18 stays unflagged.
\image(figures/anomaly_toy_threshold.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Nearest-rank selection and the later strict flag comparison are distinct operations.)
\alttext(Twenty ordered scores, the threshold18 line and the only strictly greater score highlighted.)

> Tied ranking groups do not receive an optimistic ordering

Nominal scores [1,2] and anomaly scores [2,3] have four cross-pool comparisons. The anomaly2
beats nominal1 and ties nominal2; anomaly3 beats both. AUROC is3.5/4=.875. Descending tied
groups give recall increments1/2 and1/2 at precision1 and2/3, so noninterpolated AP is5/6.
The threshold2 flags no nominal case and only anomaly3. A constant-score rule has AUROC.5
and AP equal to the supplied anomaly prevalence; equal pools here give AP baseline.5.
The native adapter reuses the canonical tied ROC/AP functions, following their
[ROC](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.roc_auc_score.html)
and [noninterpolated AP](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.average_precision_score.html) conventions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/anomaly_toy_ranking.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  const auto r = n::models::RankAnomalies(n::tensor({1., 2.}, {2}), n::tensor({2., 3.}, {2}), 2);
  std::print(
      "AUROC {:.6f}; AP {:.6f}; strict FPR {:.1f}, TPR {:.1f}.\n",
      r.auroc,
      r.average_precision,
      r.normal_fpr,
      r.anomaly_tpr);
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines({0, 0, .5, 1}, {0, .5, 1, 1}, "Grouped ROC", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .lines({0, 1}, {0, 1}, "Chance", {100, 116, 139}, 1.)
      .points({r.normal_fpr}, {r.anomaly_tpr}, "Threshold2", {220, 38, 38}, 5.)
      .x_limits(-.05, 1.05)
      .y_limits(-.05, 1.3)
      .x_label("Nominal false-positive fraction")
      .y_label("Anomaly true-positive fraction")
      .title("A tied score group contributes half credit to AUROC")
      .save_svg("build/anomaly_toy_ranking.svg");
}
```
