> Score distributions show why a threshold can miss a corruption

The following curves connect exact empirical cumulative fractions at sorted observations;
connecting segments are visual guides between observations. All200 cases of each pool remain.
Thresholds come from nominal
validation only. Each rule has its own score units and threshold; they are not put on a shared
numerical scale. Vertical plot space above fraction1 keeps legends clear of the curves.
The autoencoder's darkened-image residuals often fall below nominal residuals, so the strict
upper-tail flag misses almost all of them. The fitting-mean residual reverses darkening even
more strongly. Ink deviation directly measures brightness and behaves differently.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/anomaly_ae_cdf.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <map>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/anomaly/analysis.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  const std::string score     = "ae";
  const double      threshold = n::models::NominalThreshold(a.at("validation_" + score + "_score"));
  const std::vector<std::string> pools{"validation", "test", "patch", "darkening", "shift"},
      labels{"Calibration", "Nominal test", "White patch", "Darkening", "Right shift"};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{
      {100, 116, 139}, {37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}, {147, 51, 234}};
  const auto fraction = n::arange(1, 201, 1, n::DType::Float64) / 200.;
  auto       plot     = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
    const auto values  = a.at(pools[i] + "_" + score + "_score"),
               ordered = n::gather(values, n::argsort(values));
    plot.lines(ordered.to_vector<double>(), fraction.to_vector<double>(), labels[i], colors[i], 2.);
  }
  plot.lines({threshold, threshold}, {0, 1}, "95% threshold", {0, 0, 0}, 1.5)
      .y_limits(-.03, 1.55)
      .y_ticks({0, .25, .5, .75, 1}, {"0", ".25", ".50", ".75", "1"})
      .x_label("Autoencoder per-case residual")
      .y_label("Empirical fraction at or below score")
      .title("Autoencoder per-case residual: all fixed cases")
      .save_svg("build/anomaly_ae_cdf.svg");
}
```
