> Fidelity and scope

The canonical API owns per-case residual/ink arithmetic, explicit nearest-rank calibration,
canonical ROC/AP adaptation and detached fixed stress transforms. The report owns the visible
prerequisite, pool selection, threshold policy, complete artifact IO and figures. Both original
archives/3,198,145 values, all nine TSV rows, JSON values and ten original PNG strips are
preserved exactly. Initial/selected prerequisite checkpoints reproduce101,984 parameter values;
application inference checks all50,992 model values for immutability and adds zero updates.
Timing of the prerequisite is measured anew.

An optional independent NumPy development check verifies1,568,784 forward values,6,001 exact
scores and470,400 exact corrupted pixels, fitting-reference accumulation, all thresholds and
strict/tied controls. Maximum widened forward error is below3.6e-7. It prepares no data and
fits no model. These synthetic paired stress results do not establish real outlier detection,
class rejection or calibrated deployment error rates. Validation reuse and unfiltered failures
remain part of the result.

> References

- R stats. [Sample Quantiles](https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/quantile.html).
  The explicit nearest-rank rule corresponds to inverse empirical-CDF selection with no fuzz.
- Scikit-learn. [ROC AUC](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.roc_auc_score.html)
  and [Average Precision](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.average_precision_score.html).
  Ranking uses canonical tied comparisons and noninterpolated group-endpoint AP.
